<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle not well tested - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle not well tested - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Steers and heifers were not well tested near midday Thursday on a dressed basis delivered, paid on hot carcass weights, USDA said.</p>
<p>Dressed Basis Steers - No confirmed sales.</p>
<p>Dressed Basis Heifers - Few lots Select and Choice 2-3</p>
<p>1100-1125 lbs 118.50-119.00.</p>
<p>Slaughter steers and heifers not established. Buyer</p>
<p>inquiry fair; but most showlists already traded.  Live basis</p>
<p>sales - Equivalent 3 percent shrink delivered and FOB, some</p>
<p>FOB 4% shrink.</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers -  No confirmed sales.</p>
<p>Slaughter Heifers - No confirmed sales.</p>
<p>Confirmed - 400   For the week - 75,400</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720</p>
</text>
